gotochanger (0.4.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Redesign tape/cartridge identity and creation. "Volume label" is
    retired: Volume.Label and the old cosmetic Volume.Barcode field are
    merged into one Barcode identifier, used everywhere (filenames,
    uniqueness key, REST API, CLI). Every tape type now defines a real
    per-family barcode format (new internal/barcode package): LTO/DLT/
    SDLT follow published vendor specs, DDS/AIT/3592 use gotochanger's
    own documented convention (no external standard exists for them).
    The default tape-type catalog grew from 5 to 28 entries covering
    LTO-1 through LTO-9 (+ Type M), DLT-III/IV, SDLT-220/600, DDS-1
    through DDS-4 (+ DAT-72/160/320), AIT-1 through AIT-4, SAIT-1, and
    IBM-3592. Every cartridge must now belong to a Tape Set; the old
    free-standing "create an outside volume with any label" path
    (POST /api/v1/outside, outside-create) is removed in favor of
    tape-set-scoped creation (POST /api/v1/tape-sets with a required
    initial_tape_count, and new POST /api/v1/tape-sets/{name}/tapes for
    bulk auto-generation or a single manually-numbered cartridge).
    Barcode uniqueness is enforced globally across the whole system, not
    per tape set. A new GET /api/v1/fs/browse endpoint backs a real
    folder-picker UI component for tape-set storage folders, replacing a
    free-typed path input, in both Admin > Tape Sets and the setup
    wizard. The old global "auto-generate barcodes"/"barcode prefix"
    Settings toggle is removed, superseded by per-tape-type format.
    Breaking change: upgrading an install with existing volumes created
    before tape sets existed (e.g. bareos-disk-sd-int-fr1's 0001-0004)
    will not preserve their old label/barcode identity - this was a
    deliberate scope decision, not an oversight; see CLAUDE.md's "Real
    deployment" section before upgrading that host.
  * Fix a pre-existing tape-type row (e.g. "LTO-8", seeded by every
    install prior to this release) surviving the tape_types schema
    migration with a permissive-but-wrong generic barcode format instead
    of its real one, so cartridges created against it got plain numeric
    barcodes instead of the correct family shape. Found immediately on
    first deploy to bareos-disk-sd-int-fr1. Fixed by
    repairLegacyTapeTypeBarcodeFormats, which recognizes known legacy
    tape-type names on every startup and upgrades them to their real
    format; see CLAUDE.md's "Known gotchas" #12 for the full root cause.
    Does not rename any cartridge already created under the wrong
    format - only affects tape types going forward.

