gotochanger (0.2.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Move all library topology (drive/tape types, magazines, drive
    devices, logical libraries, tape sets, and the settings that go with
    them) from config.yaml into the SQLite database at <data_dir>/state.db
    (internal/store/topology.go). This is a clean break, not a migration:
    an existing install's config.yaml topology is ignored after upgrading
    and the setup wizard must be re-run. A fresh install now genuinely
    starts with zero drives/magazines/I-O slots configured.
  * Fix the wizard's most fundamental bug: UpdateWizardState set
    CurrentStep to the step just submitted instead of advancing past it,
    so clicking Next never actually progressed, on any step, for anyone.
  * Wizard progress (current step + completed flag) now persists across a
    daemon restart; each step's data is written straight into its final
    table/setting the moment it's submitted, so a restart mid-wizard
    resumes exactly where it left off.
  * Wizard completion now hot-applies the new topology to the running
    daemon (Library.Reconfigure) instead of only updating an in-memory
    config copy that was never actually used.
  * Add real CRUD (API, CLI, Admin UI) for drive types, tape types, tape
    sets (grouped by tape type, each with its own storage folder), and
    magazines - previously only settable once via the wizard, and in the
    case of tape sets, silently discarded on completion.
  * Add Logical Libraries as a first-class, persisted concept: partitions
    of the physical library (drives/magazines/I-O slots + a display
    color), enforced with exclusivity (an element belongs to at most one
    logical library) and runtime scoping (Load/Unload/Move reject an
    element outside the X-Logical-Library-scoped library). Add an
    "unassigned objects" view for reassignment.
  * gotochanger-changer: replace the ambiguous trailing-argument logical-
    library heuristic (which could misread a load/unload volume label as
    a library name) with an explicit --logical-library=NAME flag.
  * Add an offsite vault: manual send/recall operations plus an optional
    scheduled auto-rotation, simulating tape rotation/vaulting.
  * Latency simulation is now actually applied to Move/Load/Unload
    (previously modeled but never used to delay anything).
  * Seed the suggested drive/tape type catalog with DDS and DLT in
    addition to LTO-8/LTO-9/Unlimited.
  * Enforce magazine ID and logical library name uniqueness via SQLite
    UNIQUE constraints.
  * Drive bandwidth throttling was evaluated and deliberately not
    implemented: the symlink-based drive model never sees Bareos's byte
    stream, so there's nothing to throttle without a FUSE/kernel-device
    interception layer (the same prerequisite as the out-of-scope Kernel
    mode).
  * Wizard UX pass based on operator feedback: step 1 now requires a VTL
    (Virtual Tape Library) name; step 2's drive-type checkboxes (which
    could only pick each type once) are replaced with Add/Remove rows,
    each with its own drive-type dropdown, so multiple drives of the same
    type can be added. I/O slots are replaced throughout with Mailboxes,
    a real first-class entity mirroring Magazine exactly (own ID + slot
    count 1-5, real backend grouping, own CRUD/API/CLI/Admin UI screen)
    instead of a flat count - step 4 is now an Add/Remove-rows UI like
    step 3's magazines, and logical libraries are now assigned whole
    mailboxes by ID (like magazines) instead of individual I/O slot
    indices. Tape sets (step 6) gained a tape count field that
    auto-generates that many cartridges on wizard completion, labeled
    sequentially from the tape type (e.g. LTO-8 -> LTO800001, LTO800002,
    ...).

 -- Sebastien WENSKE <sebastien@wenske.fr>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 23:30:00 +0000

gotochanger (0.1.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix I/O (import/export) slot addressing: they were numbered as a
    separate 1..N space, invisible to Bareos/mtx-changer, which expect a
    single combined address range (storage slots first, I/O slots
    continuing right after) and learn the *total* count from the
    changer's "slots" command. gotochanger-changer's "slots" command now
    returns storage+I/O combined, matching mtx-changer's behavior of
    parsing real mtx's "N Slots (M Import/Export)" total. I/O slot
    addresses are now displayed with a trailing "@" (e.g. "21@") in
    gotochangerctl and the web UI, matching real tape library tooling.

 -- Sebastien WENSKE <sebastien@wenske.fr>  Wed, 08 Jul 2026 20:40:00 +0000

gotochanger (0.1.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix systemd UMask (0027 -> 0007): it was silently stripping the
    intentional group-write bit from volume files/directories (created
    0660/0770), breaking real read/write sharing with a service account
    added to the "gotochanger" group (e.g. bareos), as documented.

 -- Sebastien WENSKE <sebastien@wenske.fr>  Wed, 08 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0000

gotochanger (0.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: virtual tape autochanger simulator with storage
    slots, I/O (import/export) slots, virtual drives, REST API, embedded
    management web UI, gotochanger-changer (Bareos disk-changer.in
    compatible shim), gotochangerctl admin CLI and SNMPv2c trap
    notifications.

 -- Sebastien WENSKE <sebastien@wenske.fr>  Wed, 08 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
